content.text:
Here are 5 active YC companies from the directory's Developer Tools category that build tools for AI agents:

```json
[
  {
    "name": "Agent Relay",
    "website": "https://agentrelay.com/",
    "yc_page": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/agent-relay",
    "what_it_does": "Lets AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor) message each other directly, with shared, searchable session history."
  },
  {
    "name": "Herdr",
    "website": "https://herdr.dev/",
    "yc_page": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/herdr",
    "what_it_does": "Open-source runtime that keeps fleets of coding agents running across machines and tracks which are working, blocked, or done."
  },
  {
    "name": "Pomerado",
    "website": "https://www.pomerado.ai/",
    "yc_page": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/pomerado",
    "what_it_does": "Turns any website, legacy portal, or internal tool into an API or MCP server so agents can use it."
  },
  {
    "name": "Maritime",
    "website": "https://maritime.sh/",
    "yc_page": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/maritime",
    "what_it_does": "Managed cloud platform for running thousands of AI agents, each in its own isolated, persistent computer."
  },
  {
    "name": "Boxes (boxesdev)",
    "website": "https://boxes.dev/",
    "yc_page": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/boxesdev",
    "what_it_does": "Cloud VMs and sandboxes where agents can work for long periods on code or knowledge work."
  }
]
```

I took the websites from each company's YC profile page. I matched the Boxes entry to its YC listing from the page text, but I didn't open its YC page to confirm that the "Boat" description belongs to it.

